# LF in the repository and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without `eol=lf`, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true checks files out as CRLF while stylua
# writes LF (its line_endings default is Unix), so `npm run lint:stylua` reports every checked-out
# file as a whole-file diff and the check is unusable locally. This matches the `end_of_line = lf`
# the templates' .editorconfig already declares.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.rbxl binary
*.rbxm binary
